  "body": {
    "id": "thm:uniform-sandwich-ellipse",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "If Open-ended Question 7 is resolved affirmatively, then for every fixed \\(0<\\gamma<1\\), the feasible ellipse satisfies \\[\\sup_{m\\in\\mathfrak M_6}\\left|P_m\\{\\theta(m)\\in\\mathcal C_{n,m}(1-\\gamma)\\}-(1-\\gamma)\\right|\\longrightarrow0.\\] Plug-in estimates consistently estimate \\(|D(P_m)|\\), \\(\\sigma_{\\min}(J_m)\\), and \\(\\lambda_{\\min}(S_m)\\) uniformly over \\(m\\in\\mathfrak M_6\\), thereby reporting proximity to a declared strong-chart boundary without diagnosing nonidentification on the chart complement.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "n",
      "gamma",
      "m",
      "M6",
      "Pm",
      "thetam",
      "Cn",
      "D",
      "J",
      "S"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "thm:uniform-feasible-gmm",
      "def:sandwich-ellipse"
    ],
    "justification": "Coverage, rather than asymptotic normality alone, is the operational inference guarantee for the identified query.",
    "gap": "Tramontano, Drton, and Etesami explicitly leave confidence intervals open; nearby cumulant papers do not give uniform chart-aware coverage.",
    "consumer": "The ellipse and three margins can be exposed directly in software that reports outer-coefficient estimates.",
    "proof_tex": "The affirmative resolution of Open-ended Question \\(\\mathrm{oeq:uniform\\mbox{-}feasible\\mbox{-}gmm}\\) gives both the uniform \\(\\chi^2_2\\) limit with \\(V_m\\) and \\(\\widehat V_{n,m}-V_m=o_{P_m}(1)\\) uniformly. Its proof also supplies constants \\(0<c<C<\\infty\\) for which\n\\[\ncI_2\\preceq V_m\\preceq CI_2\n\\quad\\text{uniformly in }m.\n\\]\nTherefore replacing \\(V_m^{-1}\\) by \\(\\widehat V_{n,m}^{-1}\\) changes the Wald quadratic form by \\(o_{P_m}(1)\\) uniformly. At the continuous quantile \\(\\chi^2_{2,1-\\gamma}\\),\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nP_m\\{\\theta(m)\\in\\mathcal C_{n,m}(1-\\gamma)\\}\n&=P_m\\!\\left\\{n(\\widehat\\theta_{n,m}-\\theta(m))^\\top\n\\widehat V_{n,m}^{-1}(\\widehat\\theta_{n,m}-\\theta(m))\n\\le\\chi^2_{2,1-\\gamma}\\right\\}\\\\\n&=1-\\gamma+o(1),\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nwhere the remainder is uniform over \\(m\\in\\mathfrak M_6\\). Taking the supremum proves the coverage claim.\n\nFor the diagnostics, let \\(\\widehat D_{n,m}\\) be the polynomial \\(D\\) evaluated at the empirical centered cumulants. The finite-dimensional uniform moment law proved in the GMM theorem and polynomial continuity give\n\\[\n\\sup_mP_m\\bigl(|\\widehat D_{n,m}-D(P_m)|>\\epsilon\\bigr)\\to0.\n\\]\nThe reverse triangle inequality transfers this to \\(|\\widehat D_{n,m}|\\). The same theorem gives \\(\\widehat J_{n,m}-J_m=o_{P_m}(1)\\) and \\(\\widehat S_{n,m}-S_m=o_{P_m}(1)\\) uniformly. For symmetric matrices and singular values,\n\\[\n|\\sigma_{\\min}(A)-\\sigma_{\\min}(B)|\\le\\|A-B\\|,\n\\qquad\n|\\lambda_{\\min}(A)-\\lambda_{\\min}(B)|\\le\\|A-B\\|.\n\\]\nThus the plug-in smallest singular value and smallest eigenvalue consistently estimate the declared Jacobian and influence-covariance margins uniformly. These convergences only measure distance to the boundary of this sufficient chart. Because no converse statement is made on \\(D=0\\), they do not diagnose nonidentification on the chart complement.",
